{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "heat_1d_varcoeff_neumann",
    "description": "MMS driver: 1-D VARIABLE-COEFFICIENT heat equation u_t = div(k(x) grad u) + S(x,t) on the unit interval [0, 1] with inhomogeneous NEUMANN (fixed-flux) boundaries, discretized by the conservative finite-volume rule grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_laplacian_neumann_bc. The consumer writes the operator as the conservative compound D(k*D(u,x),x) (coefficient on the LEFT), which that rule matches at priority 10 and lowers to the arithmetic-mean flux-difference stencil with the domain-boundary face flux prescribed directly. The coefficient k(x) = 1 + 0.5 cos(2 pi x) is a consumer-supplied observed of shape [x] (positive on [0,1], range [0.5,1.5]); it is read by the rule body at the interior faces via kf[i+1/2]=(k[i]+k[i+1])/2. Manufactured solution u(x,t) = exp(-0.75 pi^2 t) cos(pi x) + x: the decaying cosine has u_x = -pi exp(...) sin(pi x) vanishing at both walls, while the steady ramp x contributes a constant unit gradient u_x = 1 at x=0 and x=1. Since k(0) = k(1) = 1 + 0.5 cos(0) = 1 + 0.5 cos(2 pi) = 1.5, the physical wall FLUX k u_x = 1.5 * 1 = 1.5 is constant in time at both walls, prescribed to the rule's free names qL = qR = 1.5 (the flux, not the gradient; the rule reduces to varcoeff_laplacian_zero_flux_bc at qL=qR=0). Because neither mode is an eigenfunction of the variable-coefficient operator, a forcing term S(x,t) = u_t - div(k grad u) is added so u is exact for the continuous PDE. Derivation: with k' = -pi sin(2 pi x), div(k grad u) = exp(-0.75 pi^2 t)[-0.75 pi^2 cos(pi x) - 0.75 pi^2 cos(3 pi x)] + k' (the ramp contributes div(k grad x) = k'); u_t = -0.75 pi^2 exp(-0.75 pi^2 t) cos(pi x); choosing lambda = 0.75 pi^2 cancels the cos(pi x) terms, leaving the closed form S(x,t) = exp(-0.75 pi^2 t) 0.75 pi^2 cos(3 pi x) + pi sin(2 pi x) (the steady term pi sin(2 pi x) = -k' cancels the ramp's div contribution), spelled below as a time factor exp(-0.75 pi^2 t) times a cos(3 pi x) aggregate plus a steady sin(2 pi x) aggregate. The grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0,1]: x0 = 0 (parameter) and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing by the metaparameter name N, substituted at load per esm-spec 9.7.6). qL/qR appear only in the runtime rule body; initial condition, coefficient, forcing, and test references all spell the cell-center coordinate x_i = (i - 1/2)/N inline with load-foldable scalars (AGENTS.md build-time scope caveat), with the ramp coefficient 1.0 and the flux 1.5 matching what the runtime rule reads. The SAME rule also serves the nonlinear case (a consumer declaring k as an observed k=f(u)); this driver exercises the variable-coefficient dual.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:problem", "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d", "equation:heat", "mms"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.15 (variable-coefficient conservative form) and Section 2.12 (Neumann boundary conditions by prescribing the domain-face flux)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Heat": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        { "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_laplacian_neumann_bc.esm" }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": ["x"],
          "description": "Temperature field over the x index set."
        },
        "qL": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K*m/s",
          "default": 1.5,
          "description": "Prescribed PHYSICAL FLUX k du/dx (in the +x direction) at the left wall x=x0 (the rule's Neumann free name), equal to the manufactured wall flux k(0)*u_x(0) = 1.5 * 1 = 1.5."
        },
        "qR": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K*m/s",
          "default": 1.5,
          "description": "Prescribed PHYSICAL FLUX k du/dx (in the +x direction) at the right wall x=x0+N*dx (the rule's Neumann free name), equal to the manufactured wall flux k(1)*u_x(1) = 1.5 * 1 = 1.5."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m",
          "expression": { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] },
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "k": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "m^2/s",
          "shape": ["x"],
          "description": "Variable conductivity k(x) = 1 + 0.5 cos(2 pi x) over the x index set, evaluated at cell centers x_gi = (gi - 1/2)/N (spelled inline from literals and the metaparameter name N). Positive on [0,1] (range [0.5,1.5]); k(0)=k(1)=1.5. Bound by the rule's match as the coefficient k (the left factor of k*D(u,x)) and read by the expanded interior stencil at the faces. The aggregate loops over `gi`, NOT the stencil's interior index `i`: an array coefficient authored as an aggregate observed is inlined into the stencil's [2,N-1] aggregate at evaluation, and a shared loop-index name would be captured (see the rule description).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["gi"],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": { "gi": { "from": "x" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                1.0,
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.5,
                    {
                      "op": "cos",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            6.283185307179586,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                { "op": "-", "args": ["gi", 0.5] },
                                { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "ic", "args": ["u"] },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["i"],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "cos",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "*", "args": [3.141592653589793, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }] }
                  ]
                },
                { "op": "*", "args": [1.0, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }] }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "t" },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "D",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      "k",
                      { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "x" }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "wrt": "x"
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "exp",
                    "args": [
                      { "op": "*", "args": [-7.402203300817019, "t"] }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "aggregate",
                    "output_idx": ["i"],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        7.402203300817019,
                        {
                          "op": "cos",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                9.42477796076938,
                                {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] },
                                    { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": ["i"],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    3.141592653589793,
                    {
                      "op": "sin",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            6.283185307179586,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] },
                                { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_varcoeff_neumann_decay",
          "description": "Manufactured solution u(x,t) = exp(-0.75 pi^2 t) cos(pi x) + x for u_t = div(k(x) grad u) + S(x,t) with k(x) = 1 + 0.5 cos(2 pi x), qL = qR = 1.5. Derivation: div(k grad u) = exp(-0.75 pi^2 t)[-0.75 pi^2 cos(pi x) - 0.75 pi^2 cos(3 pi x)] + k'; u_t = -0.75 pi^2 exp(-0.75 pi^2 t) cos(pi x); the forcing S = u_t - div(k grad u) = exp(-0.75 pi^2 t) 0.75 pi^2 cos(3 pi x) + pi sin(2 pi x) matches the rhs terms above, so u solves the continuous PDE exactly. The cosine mode has zero wall gradient, and the ramp x carries the constant wall gradient 1, so the physical wall flux k u_x = 1.5 is constant in time, prescribed to the rule as qL = qR = 1.5. References evaluate at cell centers x_i = (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and the metaparameter N only; the ramp coefficient 1.0 and flux 1.5 match the runtime rule). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.1 assertion bounds the relative L2 discretization error, which falls at the conservative-FV order 2. Exact per-resolution error values are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/heat_1d_varcoeff_neumann/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.1 },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 1e-9 },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": ["i"],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "cos",
                      "args": [
                        { "op": "*", "args": [3.141592653589793, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }] }
                      ]
                    },
                    { "op": "*", "args": [1.0, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }] }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 2e-3 },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": ["i"],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" } },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        { "op": "exp", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": [-7.402203300817019, 0.1] }] },
                        {
                          "op": "cos",
                          "args": [
                            { "op": "*", "args": [3.141592653589793, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }] }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    { "op": "*", "args": [1.0, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "N"] }] }] }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
